column84:
I think the current way to write that is to either use Google Guave ImmutableMap.of("a", 1, "b", 2, "c", 3) or when mutable maps are required, to write:
Map m = new HashMap() {{
put("a", 1);
put("b", 2);
put("c", 3);
}};<p>Both of these are a bit lighter yet still far away from JavaScript or Ruby special syntaxes.
